description:
Objective: under the protected profile, the VS Code extension applies the same runtime-selection rules as JetBrains:
- a strict, fail-closed profile read;
- installed-only daemon, proxy and wrapper selection;
- MOE_DAEMON_PATH, MOE_PROXY_PATH and MOE_RUNTIME_PROTECTED=1 (CQ-R13c1's marker) passed to agent launches;
- refusal instead of fallback.
This is CQ-R01 follow-up 7. JetBrains stays primary, so this row follows CQ-RF01..RF04 and CQ-R13c1, and mirrors their final behavior.

Created by architect-e4b7eee0 on 2026-10-30, when the human moved the non-gating R01 follow-ups out of CQ-R13.

Deliverable:
- The moe-vscode daemon spawn and agent launch paths implement the rules above under the protected profile.
- The legacy profile is unchanged.
- Add a unit test for the selection, and keep the startup regression tests passing.

Out of scope:
- JetBrains changes;
- persistent provenance for VS Code, unless CQ-RF01's store is shareable as-is (note it if so);
- .moe edits;
- enabling verified-local.

Verification command (fresh, exit 0 required): cd moe-vscode && npm test && npm run compile

implementationPlan.description:
In moe-vscode/src/services/MoeDaemonClient.ts, add an exported section 'Protected runtime selection', a mirror of JetBrains RuntimeSelectionPolicy (CQ-R01). It lives here, not in a new module, because five harnesses transpile this file alone with a closed require shim: daemon-start, daemon-json-cap, approval-paths, plan-approval-client and settings-wire. A new local import would break them. CQ-RF06b (task-032c9739) consumes the same exports for the daemon spawn.

Add:
- `export type RuntimeProfile = 'legacy' | 'protected'`.
- A module-level pinned Set<string>.
- `export const defaultFoldCase = process.platform === 'win32' || process.platform === 'darwin'`.
- `export function comparablePath(p, foldCase)`:
  - '\\' becomes '/';
  - a leading `//?/` or `//./` goes, with `//?/UNC/x` becoming `//x`;
  - trailing '/' goes, except on '/' or `X:/`;
  - folding is toUpperCase().toLowerCase().
- `export function isWithin(child, parent)`: true for equality, or a prefix that ends on a segment boundary.
- `export function installedRoot(extensionPath)` = path.join(extensionPath, 'bundled').
- `export function runtimeProfile(basePath): RuntimeProfile`, which never throws:
  - a blank basePath is 'legacy';
  - the key is comparablePath(realpath, else path.resolve, defaultFoldCase), and a pinned key is 'protected';
  - fs.lstatSync on <basePath>/.moe/project.json: only ENOENT means absent, which is 'legacy';
  - read through one descriptor with a 1 MiB + 1 cap (the readDaemonJsonText pattern, with the fd closed in finally); oversize is untrusted;
  - decode UTF-8; a first char U+FEFF is untrusted, since Buffer#toString keeps it;
  - JSON.parse;
  - a root that is not a plain non-array object is untrusted;
  - an own property 'settings' that is absent is 'legacy'; present but not a plain object is untrusted;
  - an own property 'executionProfile' that is absent is 'legacy'; 'legacy' and 'observe' are 'legacy'; 'verified-local' adds the key to pinned and returns 'protected'; anything else, null included, is untrusted;
  - untrusted means 'protected', unpinned, with one log line 'Moe runtime selection fails closed to the protected profile: <reason>'.
- `export function installedArtifact(root, relative, basePath, foldCase = defaultFoldCase): { accepted: string } | { rejected: string }`, with label `installed ${relative}`:
  - realpath(root) fails: 'installed Moe runtime not found';
  - realpath(basePath) fails: 'the project directory cannot be resolved';
  - realpath(join) gives ENOENT: '<label> not found'; any other error: '<label> cannot be resolved';
  - not statSync().isFile(): '<label> is not a regular file';
  - not isWithin the real root, compared EXACT and unfolded: '<label> resolves outside the installed Moe runtime';
  - isWithin the real project, compared folded: '<label> resolves inside the project';
  - otherwise { accepted: real }.

Error handling: every fs or parse failure is caught and becomes 'protected' or a rejection; nothing throws to callers. A reason reaches the UI; the absolute path goes only to log(). No existing behaviour of this file changes.
